outcomeRecord: "---\nslug: unified-toon-config\nshipped: 2026-10-16\nschemaVersion: 1\ndraft: true\n---\n# unified-toon-config\n\nDraft only: content judgment is still required.\nRead the collected evidence before choosing durable destinations.\nNo upgrade or coverage decision has been applied.\n\n- outcome: needs-decision\n- docs: none\n- decisions: none\n- knowledge: none\n- code: none\n- verification: none\n- followups: none\n- archive: none\n"
evidence[1]{path,hash,excerpt,truncated}:
  ".project/done-work.md#unified-toon-config","sha256:fabf47add794c650d2769e2f7107773c296b5d86e94e2acb858c3b9160784c38","## unified-toon-config — shipped 2026-10-16\n\nAll workflow configuration moved into one root `ai-workflow.toon` (v2.25.0, big-batch, 2026-10-16; schemaVersion 2 after an unplanned owner redesign that nested Orca under `integrations.orca` with per-coordinator `workers`). Scopes: a1 `runtime/config.mts` primitives (a strict in-repo TOON subset parser with line and column errors, `inspectPath`, `readBoundedFile`, `wxRename`, `oexLock`, `loadConfig`, `errorCodes`, and named registrar slots for integration, engine and coordinator validators), plus the pinned grammar decision `.project/decisions/toon-subset-grammar.md`, the example toon and the relocated env example; a2 seven parser-guard mutants asserting on literal `errorCodes.*` (prototype pollution, within-role duplicate, unrecognised key, EACCES, 64 KiB oversize, symlinked leaf, quoted-comma regexp backtracking); a3 five writer and path mutants, alias tests, lock tests, subprocess revalidation and the TOON fixture writer in `test-helpers.mts`; c1.1 and c1.2 readers on `loadConfig` (`env.mts` `loadConfigEnv`, `select.mts`, `entry.mts`, `orca-policy.mts` TOON-first through `policyFromConfig` into the shared `validatePolicy`, grader writes through `wxRename`), eleven reader-test files and no-race grader tests; c2.1–c2.4 the doctor \"Config validators\" check, the setup-validator \"Workflow config\" check, README/AGENTS/CLAUDE rewrites (identical), six framework docs and the build skill mirrors, hook cutover notes; b1–b3 `config-migrate.mts` (dry-run and `--apply`, three `--force` branches, dual-hash tracking, `.rejected` move-aside, legacy files never deleted; 50+ tests on Node and Bun, 20 mutants killed) and bundle-sync \"toon is never synced\" checks; d the legacy window note, the modes cutover (`loadModes` toon-first), orphaned docs and flags; reshape to `integrations.orca` and schemaVersion 2. Version 2.24.0 landed in c2.2 and 2.25.0 at ship.\n\nNo-gos held: legacy files are never deleted by the migrator; no `flock` (an O_EX",true
